***************************** T A L Y S **************************1325 1451  159
                                                                  1325 1451  160
TALYS is a computer code system for the prediction and analysis   1325 1451  161
of nuclear reactions. TALYS simulates reactions that involve      1325 1451  162
neutrons, gamma-rays, protons, deuterons, tritons, helions and    1325 1451  163
alpha-particles, in the 1 keV - 200 MeV energy range. This is     1325 1451  164
achieved by implementing a suite of nuclear reaction models into  1325 1451  165
a single code system. This nuclear data file is based on a        1325 1451  166
theoretical analysis that utilizes the optical model, compound    1325 1451  167
nucleus statistical theory, fission, direct reactions and         1325 1451  168
pre-equilibrium processes, in combination with databases and      1325 1451  169
models for nuclear structure. The following output of TALYS is    1325 1451  170
stored in this data file:                                         1325 1451  171
                                                                  1325 1451  172
- Total, elastic and non-elastic cross sections                   1325 1451  173
- Inelastic cross sections to discrete states                     1325 1451  174
- Exclusive channel cross sections, e.g. (n,g), (n,2n), (n,np),.. 1325 1451  175
- Inelastic scattering angular distributions to discrete states   1325 1451  176
- Exclusive channel energy spectra                                1325 1451  177
- Exclusive channel double-differential spectra                   1325 1451  178
- Exclusive gamma production for discrete states and continuum    1325 1451  179
- Elastic scattering angular distributions                        1325 1451  180
- Recoil data                                                     1325 1451  181
- Total particle cross sections, e.g. (n,xn), (n,xp),..           1325 1451  182
- Total particle energy spectra                                   1325 1451  183
- Total particle double-differential spectra                      1325 1451  184
- Isomeric and ground state cross sections                        1325 1451  185
- Residual production cross sections                              1325 1451  186
                                                                  1325 1451  187
For a description of the used nuclear models and their            1325 1451  188
parameterization we refer to [kon19]. If for this specific        1325 1451  189
nuclide we deviate from the global parameterization, it is made   1325 1451  190
explicit above under Nuclide Specific Information.                1325 1451  191
                                                                  1325 1451  192
